<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Amr al-Dani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">981–1053</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Amr al-Dani (981–1053) was an Andalusi scholar of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quran">Quran</a>, born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, who settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denia">Dénia</a> under its ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mujahid-al-amiri">Mujahid al-Amiri</a>. He wrote more than a hundred works on Quran recitation, orthography and the seven canonical readings, of which al-Taysir became a standard textbook. His work shaped the teaching of Quranic recitation across the western Islamic world for centuries.</p></div>
